{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hey, Mr. Hale, come on in. How's your morning going, and what can I do for you?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Refills.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Refills, sure. You're hoping for a stronger painkiller too, right?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I grabbed vitals on the way in. Blood pressure was one thirty-eight over eighty-four, heart rate seventy-two. Um, pharmacy list is up whenever you want it.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Thanks, Karen. So the low back pain — bad, worse when you bend, about five-ish years?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does it shoot down the leg at all?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any numbness or weakness in the legs?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any trouble with your breathing?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Um, let me read this right. Naproxen, two hundred fifty milligrams by mouth twice daily, for his back.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Five hundred.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Huh. So you think it's five hundred, not the two fifty on the list. Do you actually take it twice a day, or miss some?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Mostly.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. Omeprazole, twenty milligrams by mouth every morning, to protect your stomach — still on that?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): And lisinopril, ten milligrams once a day, for the high blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): What about cyclobenzaprine, ten milligrams at bedtime. Still taking it?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Stopped.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): When was that?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): March.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): There was a tramadol prescription as well. Did you ever take it, even once?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Oh, hold on. Metformin, a thousand milligrams, just popped up on the household profile. Is that yours?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Wife's.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Got it, that's her diabetes medicine, not yours. Any medication allergies?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): Back trouble run in the family?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Dad.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Man, that parking lot is a mess with the rain. Did you get flooded walking in?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): I saw a little kid in a red cap just jumping in the puddles out front. That your grandson?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Grandson.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ha. Mine would've been soaked to the knees. Their game was Saturday — well, actually, maybe it was Sunday, I lose track — and the field was a swamp.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Tell me about it. My niece was supposed to pitch. She was madder about missing the popcorn than the game, I swear.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anyway. Let me press along your low back. No tenderness, and you bend forward just fine.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think this is your long-standing mechanical low back pain. I'm not prescribing oxycodone, or anything stronger.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll refill the omeprazole and the lisinopril, and I'll refill the naproxen too, but I'm not changing that dose until we sort two fifty versus five hundred.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Take it with food, don't add ibuprofen on top, and keep moving. We might check kidney bloodwork later if you stay on the naproxen, not today.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on back and see me in three months."
 ],
